Laya.jl

The Metal buffer pools, shared uploads, cached MPSGraph command-batch encoding,
and SIMD reduction techniques in ext/ are adapted from
Laya.jl's ext/LayaMetalExt.jl, distributed under the Apache License 2.0.
A copy of that license is included in licenses/Laya-Apache-2.0.txt.

JeffClient modifications include queue-local eviction, product-only MPS graphs,
RMS/L2 normalization, causal masked softmax, fused depthwise convolution,
and a SIMD recurrent DeltaNet kernel with a triangular-solve fallback.
